{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1545859-beyond-teen-drama","id":1545859,"title":"Beyond \"Teen Drama\"","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Curseborne"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-11-14T10:20:18-08:00","id":1545859,"title":"Beyond \"Teen Drama\"","content":"Something that came out if the now-closed feedback thread is a sense that all Curseborne can do is &quot;teen drama&quot;.<br /> <br /> I both do and don't get where this idea comes from.<br /> <br /> Stylistically, I completely get it. The book has very strong teenage energy. I don't especially mind that because it reminds me a lot of original Vampire so while I wouldn't call myself a fan I get a kind of nostalgic kick out of it. <br /> <br /> Mechanically, though, I have no idea how anybody could look at this game and not see near limitless flexibility (at least in terms of theme and content, if you want to be able to flip trucks or raise Zombies you're SOL).<br /> <br /> To me, Curseborne is basically a serviceable but generic resolution system (in what the Forge would once have called &quot;Simulationist by Default&quot; style) attached to a broad and flexible (if by no means perfect) system for playing a wide range of cool supernatural beings. <br /> <br /> That's it. <br /> <br /> Mechanically, ir no more supports or forces &quot;teen drama&quot; than it supports or forces &quot;murder mystery&quot; or &quot;war story&quot;. People talk about how the default playstle involves hating your family but I really don't think that's how it'll work in practice. You're strongly mechanically incentivised to treat your family as a character archetype just like in any other splat based game.<br /> <br /> I'm going to actually get running the game pretty soon but currently I don't see any reason I'd have more difficulty running this in any given style than CofD or WoD. In don't says the blank slate makes things easier (I've shay's been a bit of a Dark Eras fan and I often like to run in historical settings where the default faction setup is a hindrance as much as anything).<br /> <br /> Maybe it'll turn out that I'm missing a bunch of tools I'll miss, but I really dig think so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28625-nobody-special","name":"Nobody Special","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-14T10:55:22-08:00","id":1545863,"title":"","content":"Honestly, I don't get this as a game for teenagers and while I'm sure it is, it seems far too mature and far more written for adults.<br /> <br /> The game lists Buffy and Warrior Nun as inspirations, which is awesome.<br /> <br /> But the <i>feeling</i> I get is far more Twin Peaks, Silent Hill, and Stephen King.<br /> <br /> The essential feeling I get from Curseborne is dealing with the day to day grind of a dark supernatural world that is grinding you down as well as the fact that you have the push back. There's countless horrifying alien things that can and will destroy you as well as the humans around you. That's in addition to all the hidden horrible secrets that twist things into nightmarish reflections of your world.<br /> <br /> Basically, if I were designing a Curseborne game, I'd say that it's much more likely to have you play a middle aged writer struggling to pay the bills while investigating what is killing the local children with magical cancer than a perky Goth Girl in high school.<br /> <br /> But you can do both.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-14T13:16:49-08:00","id":1545871,"title":"","content":"While \u201cteen drama\u201d seems like a somewhat nebulous concept, I kinda get it and I kinda get how it might be associated with Curseborne. I certainly don\u2019t think that Curseborne is in any way limited to that kind of play though. In fact, Curseborne seems pretty open ended in the okay options, more so than WoD games.<br /> <br /> There are advantages and disadvantages to that, I really don\u2019t see why you couldn\u2019t tell any story in Curseborne that you could in WoD - including themes of politics, conspiracy, and so on. It might just require a little more fleshing out on the part of the SG or perhaps subsequent books. <br /> <br /> I think that it would also be trivially easy to create new families to accommodate certain ideas that players or SG may want to flesh out their own version of the setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-14T13:37:10-08:00","id":1545877,"title":"","content":"For myself I don't see Curseborne as &quot;Teen Drama&quot; either. I do see it as &quot;Supernatural slice of life&quot;.<br /> <br /> As I said, for me that's the limitations on the game. <br /> <br /> There's no political system to engage with, no places of power, no resources to gather, no great mysteries to unravel, no great antagonists to oppose, no power to seek. <br /> <br /> There is street level survival play mixed with Stephen King weirdness. While that does provide a lot of fodder to play, I'd almost argue the Steven King liminal places is far more suited to a game for mortals than having a Revenant, Werewolf and Vampire explore the house where IT lives. <br /> <br /> What I like is supernatural conflict, political machinations, ancient evils awakening and opposing truly evil reflections that cause trouble. <br /> <br /> That is *currently* harder to do in the default assumptions of the core book. <br /> <br /> It's why I started the &quot;Factions&quot; thread as I'm trying to do something by introducing what I'd like to see that could increase the scope of play.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3769-orphan81","name":"Orphan81","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3769_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"145"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-14T14:25:34-08:00","id":1545882,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Orphan81</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1545859-beyond-teen-drama?p=1545877#post1545877\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For myself I don't see Curseborne as &quot;Teen Drama&quot; either. I do see it as &quot;Supernatural slice of life&quot;.<br /> <br /> As I said, for me that's the limitations on the game.<br /> <br /> There's no political system to engage with, no places of power, no resources to gather, no great mysteries to unravel, no great antagonists to oppose, no power to seek.</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess I don't even see it as &quot;slice of life&quot; I see it as (as I kind of said in my OP) an almost completely generic system. All of the things you're describing are stuff I'd want to junk in a game *anyway* to replace with something I found more interesting.<br /> <br /> Like I'd genuinely find it easier to run a political game, or a deep mystery game, or an opposing-great-antagonists game in Curseborne than in any WoD game for the simple reason that Curseborne has simpler NPC statblocks and that's like actual gold as far as I'm concerned.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28625-nobody-special","name":"Nobody Special","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-14T16:36:09-08:00","id":1545892,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Orphan81</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1545859-beyond-teen-drama?p=1545877#post1545877\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For myself I don't see Curseborne as &quot;Teen Drama&quot; either. I do see it as &quot;Supernatural slice of life&quot;.<br /> <br /> As I said, for me that's the limitations on the game.<br /> <br /> <b>There's no political system to engage with, no places of power, no resources to gather, no great mysteries to unravel, no great antagonists to oppose, no power to seek.</b><br /> <br /> There is street level survival play mixed with Stephen King weirdness. While that does provide a lot of fodder to play, I'd almost argue the Steven King liminal places is far more suited to a game for mortals than having a Revenant, Werewolf and Vampire explore the house where IT lives.<br /> <br /> What I like is supernatural conflict, political machinations, ancient evils awakening and opposing truly evil reflections that cause trouble.<br /> <br /> That is *currently* harder to do in the default assumptions of the core book.<br /> <br /> It's why I started the &quot;Factions&quot; thread as I'm trying to do something by introducing what I'd like to see that could increase the scope of play.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel like this one line, in particular is making a very broad and sweeping generalization that doesn't actually apply to the game.<br /> <br /> 1. There is political stuff to engage with, especially given that we do have interfamily politics and groups like the Bathory, Premier, and Heirs. I also wouldn't be surprised when we finally do get a &quot;city&quot; book that we get some examples of how Accursed in a city interact.<br /> <br /> 2. No places of power seems like a really strange thing to say because the game world has dozens of dozens of examples. They're a far bigger thing than probbaly even Werewolf or Mage. There's Loopholes, Liminalities, Shattered Spaces, and a dozen examples of places infused with supernatural powers.<br /> <br /> 3. The game lists all manner of magical items that play a much bigger role in this setting than the WOD. If your characters want to loot and gain power ups, there's certainly examples. Nor is there<br /> anything stopping you from trying to be rich or powerful with your powers.<br /> <br /> 4. There's all manner of mysteries to solve from the origins of families, how to break curses, and the weirdness of the Outside.<br /> <br /> 5. The Accursed are literally up against a bunch of extra-dimensional gods. The Archons are as powerful as Antediluvians and beyond probably. You also have immortal Ratman Jack the Ripper. Plus the Ninja Nun Catholic Church. What are you looking for regarding antagonists.<br /> <br /> I mean it's not that street level when it involves extra-dimensional invasions.<br /> <br /> -CT Phipps","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-14T16:56:36-08:00","id":1545894,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1545859-beyond-teen-drama?p=1545892#post1545892\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I feel like this one line, in particular is making a very broad and sweeping generalization that doesn't actually apply to the game.<br /> <br /> 1. There is political stuff to engage with, especially given that we do have interfamily politics and groups like the Bathory, Premier, and Heirs. I also wouldn't be surprised when we finally do get a &quot;city&quot; book that we get some examples of how Accursed in a city interact.<br /> <br /> 2. No places of power seems like a really strange thing to say because the game world has dozens of dozens of examples. They're a far bigger thing than probbaly even Werewolf or Mage. There's Loopholes, Liminalities, Shattered Spaces, and a dozen examples of places infused with supernatural powers.<br /> <br /> 3. The game lists all manner of magical items that play a much bigger role in this setting than the WOD. If your characters want to loot and gain power ups, there's certainly examples. Nor is there<br /> anything stopping you from trying to be rich or powerful with your powers.<br /> <br /> 4. There's all manner of mysteries to solve from the origins of families, how to break curses, and the weirdness of the Outside.<br /> <br /> 5. The Accursed are literally up against a bunch of extra-dimensional gods. The Archons are as powerful as Antediluvians and beyond probably. You also have immortal Ratman Jack the Ripper. Plus the Ninja Nun Catholic Church. What are you looking for regarding antagonists.<br /> <br /> I mean it's not that street level when it involves extra-dimensional invasions.<br /> <br /> -CT Phipps</div> </div> </div> </div>1) We have very little information about how these families and lineages interact with one another, how any Accursed governmental structure exists.<br /> <br /> 2) Liminal Spaces are *not* Places of power. Particularly since the majority are innocuous or hostile. <br /> <br /> 3) Resources involve herds, servants, influence and magical items. Of which, no I highly disagree, there are far less magical items as opposed to wod with its fetishes, treasures, artifacts, relics and other such things. <br /> <br /> 4) There's no mystery over the origin of families. That's trying to find a mystery where there is none. Exploring liminalities can be a mystery but it's a very limited one in concept. As for breaking curses we're led to believe it's not possible. There's no ancient mysteries, no lost lineages or families, no former secret conspiracies that once existed, no real curseborne history to dive into. <br /> <br /> 5) No they're not. *SOME* Accursed are against Archons, mainly The Outcasts. The rest of the lineages can completely ignore Archons unless an St forces the issue. For that matter we have no great liminal spaces that have Archons that could potentially threaten everything given as examples and that's probably because they can't. We have no &quot;Hell&quot; for example with a powerful Demonic Archon that can threaten entire areas. As it is fighting Archons is a Outcast and specifically a Battlefield Angels sort of thing. <br /> <br /> I'm sorry but I'm just not sold on your arguments. They seem to be reaching and filling in a lot of blanks with your own interpretation of things. <br /> <br /> You can make these arguments but they're not the ones spelled out in the texts. I don't want to turn this into a bashing thread as the other one was closed, I'm simply presenting my perspective as someone whose 43 years old and has been playing these games since 1993.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3769-orphan81","name":"Orphan81","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3769_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"145"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-14T19:19:50-08:00","id":1545905,"title":"","content":"To make something constructive in topic - I point to the <b>Riverdale</b> TV series. <b>Riverdale</b> started as modern teen drama - and ended with multidimensional aliens, 25 serial killers and any one and everything being totally... Well, on heads of it. If you want to run 'fever dreams' like <b>Riverdale</b> - I suspect <b>Curseborne</b> is perfect for it. <br /> <br /> ( Whole Riverdale plot sum up in video below \ud83d\ude0e )<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://youtu.be/LsrMrAAZ5KQ?si=IBnNM_byTM1vLIau\" data-code=\"LsrMrAAZ5KQ\" data-provider=\"youtube_share\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/LsrMrAAZ5KQ/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-14T19:28:18-08:00","id":1545906,"title":"","content":"I feel that it was a big mistake going back to high school for the final season, especially when they fighting Randal Flagg.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-14T21:30:48-08:00","id":1545919,"title":"","content":"An RPG setting lives or dies on its antagonists. The main antagonists in Curseborne so far are ... the liminalities, Shattered Spaces in particular. There are hints of others (the Fae, the Archons, inter-Family rivalries) but nothing definite enough to build a campaign on. Evil places are certainly an original idea for antagonists, but you can't really get more than one story out of each - one Shattered Space doesn't coordinate its plans with another. So how <i>do</i> you put together an overarching plot in this game?<br /> <br /> Also... Twin Peaks, Silent Hill, and Stephen King's books all have <i>mundane</i> protagonists. Indeed, their relative helplessness when confronting the supernatural threats is important to the tone in them all. Starting Accursed at 1 Entanglement aren't very powerful, compared to the antagonists in the book, so you do get something of that tone. But what do you do as Entanglement rises and the PCs get more potent?<br /> <br /> The game isn't broken, by any means, but resources for the Storyguide are kind of... thin, as it stands. We'll need supplements to support anything more than standalone episodes, unrelated to each other. Which is to say, the game isn't finished yet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1133-michael-brazier","name":"Michael Brazier","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-14T22:24:25-08:00","id":1545920,"title":"","content":"Eh, there's also the fact that most horror fiction with mundane protagonists aren't going to have multiple encounters with the Supernatural.<br /> <br /> CALL OF CTHULHU investigators have such high lethality not mattering because with the exception of Masks of Nyarlathotep and a few others, there's very few games that will be full blown campaigns.<br /> <br /> And even then, there's some breathing room. A lot of Stephen King's protagonists have some form of psychic power or ability to push back the supernatural.<br /> <br /> And we'd be remiss to forget Roland who could kill the population of Delaware by himself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-14T23:22:19-08:00","id":1545921,"title":"","content":"The problem is number of unknown story elements ( because everything related to setting is in-character narration in \ud83d\ude1e ) AND power levels of Accursed. Your<b> X-Files/Stephen King</b>'s are all good for mortals plays. Hell, it's exactly what <b>CoD</b> done in corebook and <b>Hunter: The Vigi</b>l for Tier 1. But when your PCs are proper Monsters - plots about 'human eating deli stores' are looking thin in one or two sessions. That's why <b>HtV</b> in Tier 3 have whole Conspiracies, intrugies and plot hooks for orgs.<br /> <br /> I will see how Liminalities supplement will come out for <b>Curseborne</b> - but, for now, I do not see here proper chronicle/series material in corebook.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 11-15-2024, 03:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-15T07:54:25-08:00","id":1545938,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael Brazier</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1545859-beyond-teen-drama?p=1545919#post1545919\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">An RPG setting lives or dies on its antagonists. The main antagonists in Curseborne so far are ... the liminalities, Shattered Spaces in particular. There are hints of others (the Fae, the Archons, inter-Family rivalries) but nothing definite enough to build a campaign on. Evil places are certainly an original idea for antagonists, but you can't really get more than one story out of each - one Shattered Space doesn't coordinate its plans with another. So how <i>do</i> you put together an overarching plot in this game?<br /> <br /> Also... Twin Peaks, Silent Hill, and Stephen King's books all have <i>mundane</i> protagonists. Indeed, their relative helplessness when confronting the supernatural threats is important to the tone in them all. Starting Accursed at 1 Entanglement aren't very powerful, compared to the antagonists in the book, so you do get something of that tone. But what do you do as Entanglement rises and the PCs get more potent?<br /> <br /> The game isn't broken, by any means, but resources for the Storyguide are kind of... thin, as it stands. We'll need supplements to support anything more than standalone episodes, unrelated to each other. Which is to say, the game isn't finished yet.</div> </div> </div> </div>This very much gets a &quot;semi-agree&quot; from me.<br /> <br /> I don't think it's true that RPGs stand or fall in their antagonists. The default antagonist of VtM is basically just &quot;other vampires&quot; and it works fine. Sure the Antediluvians are a thing but they're irrelevant to most games and don't have actual rules (in some ways they're no more fleshed out than the Archons).<br /> <br /> Or to go even broader, the antagonist of D&amp;D is... &quot;monsters&quot;.<br /> <br /> I do think it's valid to point out that the default style Curseborne seems to be aiming at is one that makes more sense with mortal protagonists, but I think that's been at least semi-true of most games in this genre. There just isn't that much source material for horror stuff from the perspective of the monsters and when it does exist it often goes the Curseborne route, putting its monster protagonists in a similar place to mortal investigator types.<br /> <br /> Finally, I don't think I'm concerned about PCs outstripping antagonists in terms of power level. Honestly advancement in CB looks like it goes *out* more than *up*. There's not a huge amount an E4 character can do that's straight up more *powerful* than what an E1 character can do. Plus without resorting to GM Fiat, players outstripping Threats is was always a problem in *ofD games. VtM, for example, gets to rocket tag levels of power incredibly quickly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28625-nobody-special","name":"Nobody Special","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-15T08:35:13-08:00","id":1545946,"title":"","content":"I think the comparisons to VTM are kind of misplaced when saying &quot;Well, Vampire had no overarching antagonists and it was campaign worthy, so how isn't that the same as Curseborne?&quot;<br /> <br /> Vampire had lots of depth to the setting, even in that first edition. Beyond the fact comparing it to first edition vampire is extremely unfair, we've had 30 years of RPG development, we shouldn't be comparing it to 1991 Vampire. <br /> <br /> Revised or Requiem 1st would be better. <br /> <br /> But back to the point. <br /> <br /> Vampire in its core books had an intricate political system baked in that would provide conflict against those other Vampires from the starting gun. <br /> <br /> It also had things like &quot;Ghouls&quot;, and the Blood bond which through wrinkles into dealing with mortals. <br /> <br /> And then it also had The Sabbat/VII/Belials Brood. <br /> <br /> As well as more esoteric things like 0 humanity vampires and independent bloodlines. <br /> <br /> There was so much for a St to work with and hit the ground running.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3769-orphan81","name":"Orphan81","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3769_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"145"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-15T08:47:47-08:00","id":1545948,"title":"","content":"So I thought it might be worth responding to Orphan81's points specifically and addressing how I'm planning to approach each of them in my Golden Age of Piracy game, because if nothing else I think that'll highlight some of the places where these are clear preference differences, and places where maybe there's actually a ball the game is dropping.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Orphan81</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1545859-beyond-teen-drama?p=1545894#post1545894\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) We have very little information about how these families and lineages interact with one another, how any Accursed governmental structure exists.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm *super glad* it doesn't have this. Like don't get me wrong, an example or two wouldn't go amiss, but I'd want something like you got in 2nd Edition Vampire: the Requiem where it kind of went out of its way to show that (a) the default location isn't a &quot;city&quot; and (b) there fundamentally is no default &quot;governmental structure&quot;. 2E Requiem has cities with a classic &quot;Prince and Primogen&quot; setup, cities where it's all Clan no Covenant, and at least one small town setting where the shots are called by a mysterious supernatural entity that nobody has ever seen but knows better than to cross.<br /> <br /> For my forthcoming game my plan is very much to sit down and work out the political structure once my players have created their PCs, to make sure the game fits their interests. And because the game is probably going to be set in &quot;the Spanish Main&quot; rather than &quot;Chicago&quot; a default City structure doesn't really help me (not dumping on city-style games, just highlighting that as somebody who wants to use the game as a truly *flexible* horror/occult game, I get way more mileage out of pagecount devoted to flexible tools I can use in a variety of settings, rather than super-focused examples of the large-metropolis-in-modern-day setting).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2) Liminal Spaces are *not* Places of power. Particularly since the majority are innocuous or hostile. </div> </div> </div>I do agree that Liminal Spaces are a bit vaguely defined at the moment. A broad general issue I have with Curseborne as it currently stands (and this is a touch ironic for me to say as somebody who values it primarily as a kit game) is that it seems to be trying to be all things to all people. Currently &quot;Liminality&quot; is almost a term without a reference, the book is perilously close to saying that a Liminality can be <i>literally anything</i> and that's not super useful.<br /> <br /> That said I *do* think Liminalities completely fit the Places of Power criterion. It's just (and I think this is the preferences thing kicking in again), they're places of power in a way that's mostly represented by in-world effects rather than game mechanical effects. This isn't the same as Werewolf Caerns/Loci or Mage Nodes in that they're places with a game mechanical rating that gives you mechanical resources. They're more like Verges in Awakening or for that matter Regiones in Ars Magica.<br /> <br /> For the GAOP game I fully intend to have hidden seas, mysterious islands and probably cursed bits of Nassau, all of which are (a) Liminal Spaces and (b) <i>genuinely useful to interact with</i>. I think the book could include more examples of this sort of thing but to me the in-character advantage of controlling Liminalities jumps out very easily. For a start it's just straightforwardly handy to have a base of operations that mundane people literally can't go to (or can't go to easily), plus the impression I get is that Liminalities are supposed to contain a ton of ambient supernatural effects which are, again, likely to just be straight-up <i>useful</i>.<br /> <br /> Having your home base on an island that can't be reached by anybody who hasn't already been there is useful. Having your home base on an island that can't be reached by anybody who hasn't already been there <i>and also has the fountain of youth on it</i> is a game changer.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 3) Resources involve herds, servants, influence and magical items. Of which, no I highly disagree, there are far less magical items as opposed to wod with its fetishes, treasures, artifacts, relics and other such things. </div> </div> </div>This feels like a design difference between Storyteller/ing and Storypath. Herds, Influence and the like as game mechanical stats you can put points into don't seem to be part of the system, and even Wealth is decoupled from how much money you have, and has become more of a stat for how good you are at leveraging wealth you otherwise have as flavour text. This seems to be part of a broader design philosophy of game mechanical stats just representing <i>what they do in-game</i> rather than having a fixed in-universe meaning.<br /> <br /> I like that approach, but YMMV.<br /> <br /> I will say that I think Contacts and Bonds do a lot of the heavy lifting here, as do the rules for Access from Paths, so it's not like these things have no game mechanical representation, they're just filtered in a different way (a bit like CofD got rid of &quot;Influence&quot; and folded it into &quot;Contacts&quot; and &quot;Allies&quot;).<br /> <br /> For the game I'm currently planning, there's loads of space for people to have herds, influence, resources and the like. It's just that I'm expecting it all to be stuff that exists only insofar as it exists in-world. If you steal a pirate ship, now you've got a pirate ship. If you hire a crew, now you've got a crew.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 4) There's no mystery over the origin of families. That's trying to find a mystery where there is none. Exploring liminalities can be a mystery but it's a very limited one in concept. As for breaking curses we're led to believe it's not possible. There's no ancient mysteries, no lost lineages or families, no former secret conspiracies that once existed, no real curseborne history to dive into. </div> </div> </div>To be fair to CTPhipps I do think there's <i>supposed</i> to be a mystery over the origin of Families (there's a Special Capitalised Term for this - &quot;Provenance&quot; - so I think we're supposed to care about it, but I agree it doesn't come across clearly).<br /> <br /> Generally, though, I <i>actively dislike</i> canon mysteries. It just isn't useful to me to have a book that says &quot;also there's this thing that used to exist but doesn't any more and nobody knows what happened to it&quot; or &quot;there's this big important cosmological thing but nobody knows what its deal is.&quot; My absolute 100% favourite thing an RPG can do is tell me clearly what stuff I'm supposed to make up for myself as a GM and having stuff hinted at with the implication that All Will Be Revealed if I just buy enough sourcebooks puts me off a game super fast.<br /> <br /> So for my own table, the &quot;mysteries&quot; are the ones I make up myself for the players to investigate. What's the deal with the ghost ship? Did that gold really come from El Dorado? Who murdered your brother?<br /> <br /> This one really is a taste issue. I'm not going to pretend that Curseborne as presented is filled with tantalising mysteries because I don't think it is. It's just that I actively prefer it that way.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 5) No they're not. *SOME* Accursed are against Archons, mainly The Outcasts. The rest of the lineages can completely ignore Archons unless an St forces the issue. For that matter we have no great liminal spaces that have Archons that could potentially threaten everything given as examples and that's probably because they can't. We have no &quot;Hell&quot; for example with a powerful Demonic Archon that can threaten entire areas. As it is fighting Archons is a Outcast and specifically a Battlefield Angels sort of thing. </div> </div> </div>I think this one is slightly unfair, especially when you compare it to WoD games.<br /> <br /> It's true that the Archons seem quite siloed off as a thing that only the Outcasts seem to give a crap about, but my strong suspicion is that it won't work out like this in practice. Everybody can go into and interact with Liminal Spaces and Shattered Spaces, and it does seem like Archons can at least send agents into the world to mess with stuff.<br /> <br /> And when you compare Curseborne to Vampire: the Masquerade, while it's true that every clan has a founder, it's not like the Antediluvians are super relevant to most games. So I think it's reasonable to accept that the Archons are at least as relevant to CB as the Antes are to VtM. I agree they're not as present as, say, the Wyrm in Werewolf or the Technocracy in Mage but it *is* trying to be a different kind of game and I think that's okay.<br /> <br /> For my own table, I'll want to fit the antagonists to the players' preferences, which is good because that's how I like to run games anyway. And the book really does give me a ton of options there. As I think I said on the &quot;favourite antagonists&quot; thread, what I most like about the game is that it has a simple templating system that means designing my own darned antagonists should be quick and easy rather than fiddly and time consuming (statting up elder vampires in VtM is a pain).<br /> <br /> I'm absolutely not going to pretend that it does the thing you want it to do (although I'd argue that in this specific case it does it about as well as first or second edition VtM), but I do think it might simply not be trying to do that, and while it's valid to wish it had made a different creative choice, I'm kinda glad it didn't (ironically one of my biggest concerns about the game is that a few supplements down the line it'll be a whole lot more like the game you like and a whole lot less like the game I like).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28625-nobody-special","name":"Nobody Special","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-15T08:56:07-08:00","id":1545950,"title":"","content":"A repost of a section of my review of the manuscript that was influenced by this:<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <br /> <b>What do you do in the Game?</b><br /> <br /> This complicated question is answered across the entire book but comes in two parts. The first being, &quot;Whatever you want.&quot; I once described the initial success of Vampire: The Masquerade as being the game about nothing. You can get up, feed, and go down to the Succubus Club to hang out with other vampires as what you do in the game. The game recognized being a vampire or other supernatural was an inherently interesting Curseborne hasn't released its equivalent of Chicago by Night but there's plenty of fun to be had with the idea of socializing as an Addams Family or Munsters group of people.<br /> <br /> The second, more traditional, RPG part is probably best defined as, &quot;Defend your territory against the onrush of the weird.&quot; While only the Outsiders are 100% committed to fighting the Outside (Extra-Dimensional Space), the game makes it abundantly clear that Earth's veil to the Spirit World is swiss cheese rather than a brick wall. Earth is constantly being invaded by supernatural nasties that turn houses into the Overlook Hotel or the equivalent of Walmart-sized Mimics.<br /> <br /> The nature of the WOC is that as an Accursed, you are burdened with the ability to see all the monsters around you and ignoring them is not necessarily an option. Even if your characters are sociopaths, they're probably not going to happy if Chucky starts killing kids around them. You don't want to attract the wrong kind of attention after all. Much is made of holding territory as a form of status and power in the Accursed world. To hold territory means you have to defend it against the other, less pleasant supernaturals out there. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-15T12:12:46-08:00","id":1545956,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1545859-beyond-teen-drama?p=1545950#post1545950\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A repost of a section of my review of the manuscript that was influenced by this:</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm a bit concerned I'm going to come across as just playing both sides here or arguing for the sake of arguing, but I think this is actually a really strong example of why so many people are bouncing off of <i>Curseborne</i> (a game which, I'll reiterate, I'm actually enthusiastic about and am actively preparing to run).<br /> <br /> This in particular:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The nature of the WOC is that as an Accursed, you are burdened with the ability to see all the monsters around you and ignoring them is not necessarily an option. Even if your characters are sociopaths, they're probably not going to happy if Chucky starts killing kids around them. You don't want to attract the wrong kind of attention after all. Much is made of holding territory as a form of status and power in the Accursed world. To hold territory means you have to defend it against the other, less pleasant supernaturals out there. </div> </div> </div>seems to be exactly the kind of thing people are talking about when they don't see what the game is set up for beyond reactive, monster-of-the-week style gameplay. Certainly it doesn't appeal to me as an elevator pitch at all; if anything it reminds me of the absolute worst experiences I've had with Vampire the Masquerade, the games where despite all the lore and setting details, in practice what you have is a totally reactive game where some problem comes along and it's just kind of assumed that it's up to the PCs to solve it because they're PCs.<br /> <br /> What it comes down to for me is that I'll judge the success or failure of this game on whether playing a Hungry makes me feel <i>like a vampire</i> (which honestly VtM didn't always do well and VtR second did very well indeed), whether Sorcerers feel like sorcerers and the werewolves feel like werewolves.<br /> <br /> The pitch you're giving here makes it feel like no matter what Family I pick, I'm meant to be playing An Accursed (tm) which is a type of ordinary human who is cursed with the ability to see monsters and feels like they have an obligation to protect people from them. That might even be a fun thing for a game to be, but then it's wasting a ton of time and energy with all this stuff about being angels and demons and shapeshifters. Going back to Michael Brazier's point, it feels very strongly built around telling the kind of story that defaults to having mortal protagonists.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28625-nobody-special","name":"Nobody Special","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-15T12:32:05-08:00","id":1545957,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nobody Special</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1545859-beyond-teen-drama?p=1545956#post1545956\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> The pitch you're giving here makes it feel like no matter what Family I pick, I'm meant to be playing An Accursed (tm) which is a type of ordinary human who is cursed with the ability to see monsters and feels like they have an obligation to protect people from them. That might even be a fun thing for a game to be, but then it's wasting a ton of time and energy with all this stuff about being angels and demons and shapeshifters. Going back to Michael Brazier's point, it feels very strongly built around telling the kind of story that defaults to having mortal protagonists.</div> </div> </div> </div>This goes back to my other issue of the lineages not having enough mechanical distinctions between them to make them really *feel* like Vampires, Werewolves and Demons.<br /> <br /> I'm with you in that I want Curseborne to succeed, I want it to be great, but it doesn't feel like a finished game. I think a lot of us are seeing the problem with the current set up almost being more appropriate for a &quot;Mortals with psychic abilities fighting the liminal spaces and what they spit out&quot;, then a game where we play Supernatural monsters co existing and our different lineages and families actually *mean* something significant.<br /> <br /> I think I'm going to post my own version of the lineages soon, when I have a better handle on how the combat system works.<br /> <br /> Things I would do to make those lineages feel more impactful to one another.<br /> <br /> I think I'd make the Dead more like The Crow, unstoppable revenants that don't feel pain, recover easily from damage and are driven by passionate obsession.<br /> <br /> For Primals, a customizable Wild Form that gets more powerful with each level of entanglement.<br /> <br /> Outcasts all get the ability to make &quot;Pacts&quot; with Mortals, granting their wishes or imparting supernatural power. The pacted mortal then becomes a servant and source of curse energy with higher entanglement giving a greater amount of mortals that can be pacted.<br /> <br /> For the Hungry , they're pretty good with the undead might ability but I think also giving them natural weapons for eating based on family would help.<br /> <br /> And for Sorcerors? Honestly just have them start with more powers than everyone else and maybe have a slight xp discount.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3769-orphan81","name":"Orphan81","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3769_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"145"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-15T12:39:32-08:00","id":1545958,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Orphan81</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1545859-beyond-teen-drama?p=1545957#post1545957\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This goes back to my other issue of the lineages not having enough mechanical distinctions between them to make them really *feel* like Vampires, Werewolves and Demons.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>This is very much something I'm nervous about but am reserving judgement on.<br /> <br /> My plan for my upcoming game is to play it straight but to be very generous with spot rulings and non-mechanical stuff. Basically I think the game will work fine if every Family <i>formally</i> works like the Black Hearts, Ascetics and Vorare - they get a bunch of abilities that actually do mechanically affect the world, it's just that they're supposed to be the sort of thing the GM eyeballs and says &quot;yeah of course that works, why wouldn't it&quot; rather than something you have to pay points or have a system for.<br /> <br /> (For example, I won't houserule in customisable Wild Forms for Primals but I'll absolutely rule that they: get Enhancement on things their Wild Form would be unusually good at; have Natural Weapons if it seems reasonable that they'd have natural weapons; can use the special methods of locomotion their wild form would get, potentially including flight, and so on).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28625-nobody-special","name":"Nobody Special","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-15T14:34:27-08:00","id":1545966,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nobody Special</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1545859-beyond-teen-drama?p=1545956#post1545956\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">seems to be exactly the kind of thing people are talking about when they don't see what the game is set up for beyond reactive, monster-of-the-week style gameplay. Certainly it doesn't appeal to me as an elevator pitch at all; if anything it reminds me of the absolute worst experiences I've had with Vampire the Masquerade, the games where despite all the lore and setting details, in practice what you have is a totally reactive game where some problem comes along and it's just kind of assumed that it's up to the PCs to solve it because they're PCs.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, it's also got the &quot;Do whatever you want element.&quot; Personally, the thing I hope it avoids like a plague is big huge courts and politicking. Maybe you could have a single city or so do that but I'd hate it for it miss out on all its potential weirdness that way.<br /> <br /> But yes, the &quot;Monster of the Week&quot; formula seems baked into the setting because I get a very strong impression this is a MYSTERY game.<br /> <br /> Weird thing is happening, go see what it is.<br /> <br /> It's not a combat game (it could be) but definitely something influenced by trying to have the players discover shit going on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-15T15:11:59-08:00","id":1545967,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1545859-beyond-teen-drama?p=1545966#post1545966\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, it's also got the &quot;Do whatever you want element.&quot; Personally, the thing I hope it avoids like a plague is big huge courts and politicking. Maybe you could have a single city or so do that but I'd hate it for it miss out on all its potential weirdness that way.<br /> <br /> But yes, the &quot;Monster of the Week&quot; formula seems baked into the setting because I get a very strong impression this is a MYSTERY game.<br /> <br /> Weird thing is happening, go see what it is.<br /> <br /> It's not a combat game (it could be) but definitely something influenced by trying to have the players discover shit going on.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh yeah that's all valid. I'm not suggesting that you've misrepresented the game or didn't include the &quot;kit&quot; aspect, I just thought it was a good example of why some people are seeing the core pitch as really not appealing.<br /> <br /> I do also agree that &quot;big courts and politics&quot; isn't a route I especially want to see the game go down.<br /> <br /> I think for me, the issue here is that there's a certain amount of conflict between what the game pitches itself as and what it does out of the box. That in itself isn't a huge surprise because (as I've mentioned above) it kind of pitches itself as being all things to all people so it's bound to drop some balls here and there, but I think for me the key is more in realising that it's not particularly an &quot;out of the box&quot; game. I've lost count of the number of times I've used the phrase <b>Curseborne would massively benefit from clear campaign frames</b> in various fora, but, well, Curseborne would massively benefit from clear campaign frames.<br /> <br /> Out of the box, Curseborne really does kind of only do what you're describing, the my-least-favourite-kind-of-vampire, there's a thing going on and for some reason you decide it's your job to fix it, low key monster of the week story. But out of the box, D&amp;D is kind of like that too. And I don't mean that in a disparaging way, D&amp;D has proven itself over the decades to be an extremely flexible game (not quite as flexible as WotC seems to want it to be, but that's another story) and the reason for that is that its core mechanics can actually be taken in a variety of directions.<br /> <br /> Curseborne is similar, but in some ways more flexible. A while back I compared it to GURPS which I think some people took as disparaging, but I mostly meant it as a compliment. This is a game that gives you a whole lot of tools and one or two somewhat uncomfortable pieces of furniture. That's personally exactly what I want but I think a lot of people are really looking for a nice dining room set.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28625-nobody-special","name":"Nobody Special","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}